{"body":"## Summary\nReject non-finite or out-of-range mastery thresholds before loading a goal. NaN previously reported zero mastery silently; invalid thresholds now raise the documented ValueError. Finite thresholds in the inclusive interval [0, 1] preserve existing progress calculations.\n\nCloses #671\n\n## Validation\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/learners tests/mastery -q --no-cov` — 95 passed.\n- [x] `python -m mypy src/lms/learners/repository.py tests/learners/test_learners.py` — passed.\n- [x] Ruff, Black, and `git diff --check` — passed.\n- [x] Persisted-evidence cases cover NaN, both infinities, negative values, values above one, missing goals, continued session use, and valid zero/one endpoints.\n- [x] Deliberate break tested and reverted: removing the threshold guard caused all 12 invalid-input regression cases to fail; restored suite passed.\n\n<!-- deliberate-break: test=tests/learners/test_learners.py::test_goal_progress_rejects_invalid_mastery_threshold test-file=tests/learners/test_learners.py break-file=src/lms/learners/repository.py -->\n\nLocal evidence: opener run 20260919T210204Z, `deliberate-break.txt` and `tests-restored.txt`.\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:671 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #671\n\nCloses #671\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\nIn `goal_progress_for_learner` (`src/lms/learners/repository.py:308-349`), the `mastery_threshold: float` parameter is used in comparisons (`estimate_by_node.get(node_id, 0.0) >= mastery_threshold`) without validating that it is a finite float in `[0.0, 1.0]`. If `float('nan')` is passed, the comparison `x >= nan` evaluates to `False` for all nodes, silently reporting `mastered_count: 0` and `progress: 0.0` even for fully mastered goals. If non-finite (`inf`, `-inf`) or out-of-range (`-0.5`, `1.5`) values are passed, calculations produce distorted domain metrics without raising an error.\n\n#### Tasks\n1. [x] In `src/lms/learners/repository.py`, check `if not math.isfinite(mastery_threshold) or not (0.0 <= mastery_threshold <= 1.0): raise ValueError(\"mastery_threshold must be a finite float between 0.0 and 1.0 (inclusive)\")` at the beginning of `goal_progress_for_learner`.\n2. [x] In `tests/learners/test_learners.py`, add unit test cases checking `goal_progress_for_learner` with `float('nan')`, `float('inf')`, `float('-inf')`, `-0.1`, and `1.1`, verifying `ValueError` is raised.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Running `pytest tests/learners/test_learners.py` passes cleanly.\n- [x] Calling `goal_progress_for_learner(session, learner_id=..., goal_id=..., mastery_threshold=float('nan'))` raises `ValueError(\"mastery_threshold must be a finite float between 0.0 and 1.0 (inclusive)\")`.\n- [x] Calling `goal_progress_for_learner(session, learner_id=..., goal_id=..., mastery_threshold=1.5)` raises `ValueError(\"mastery_threshold must be a finite float between 0.0 and 1.0 (inclusive)\")`.\n- [x] Calling `goal_progress_for_learner(session, learner_id=..., goal_id=..., mastery_threshold=-0.1)` raises `ValueError(\"mastery_threshold must be a finite float between 0.0 and 1.0 (inclusive)\")`.\n- [x] Deliberately breaking the validation logic causes the targeted tests to fail.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Added validation for learning-goal mastery thresholds.\n  * Invalid, non-finite, or out-of-range thresholds now produce a clear validation error.\n  * Valid thresholds continue to calculate learner progress with inclusive mastery counts, including boundary values of 0 and 1.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for valid and invalid mastery threshold values.\n  * Added checks to ensure invalid thresholds are rejected before progress evaluation begins.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","closingIssuesReferences":[{"id":"I_kwDOSm8tI88AAAABQte3wQ","number":671,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOSm8tIw","name":"learning-management-system","owner":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDQ2MzIy","login":"stranske"}},"url":"https://github.com/stranske/learning-management-system/issues/671"}],"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkkwsEw","name":"agent:codex","description":"Assign to Codex agent","color":"0e8a16"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkkwsIQ","name":"agents:keepalive","description":"Enable keepalive monitoring on PR","color":"1d76db"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkkwsNg","name":"autofix","description":"Let bots format/lint automatically","color":"0366d6"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkk75eg","name":"verify:compare","description":"Runs verifier comparison mode after merge","color":"942665"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAAC0VgzwQ","name":"codex","description":"Created by Codex","color":"6f42c1"}],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"769e73eb50d2d2fc883c080276ac566a2d349b07"},"mergedAt":"2026-09-19T22:28:25Z","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-19T22:10:30Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/stranske/learning-management-system/actions/runs/35472526726/job/105976062227","name":"Evaluate keepalive loop","startedAt":"2026-09-19T22:10:30Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Agents Gate Followups"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-19T22:28:38Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/stranske/learning-management-system/actions/runs/35473438153/job/105978447772","name":"create-new-pr","startedAt":"2026-09-19T22:28:38Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Create New PR from Verification"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-19T22:09:59Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/stranske/learning-management-system/actions/runs/35472527545/job/105975987682","name":"cross-repo smoke","startedAt":"2026-09-19T22:10:00Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Cross-Repo Smoke"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-19T22:09:59Z","con